      {
        "Id": "967e5006b7a74373a22745d07bfeecbe",
        "Title": "HOW TO USE  -  1st run: leave the file empty -> <project>_LEVELS.xlsx is made next to the .rvt from your Revit levels\nThen Browse... to that Excel.  Edit names / first elevation / floor-to-floor heights, SAVE the Excel -> Revit updates by itself (Automatic mode).\nNew row = new level (+ floor and ceiling plan).  Renamed row = renamed level + its views.  Deleted row = kept in Revit unless DELETE is on.\nMatching uses the REVIT ID column, then the name, then the elevation - never doubles levels.",
        "DescriptionText": null,
        "IsExpanded": true,
        "WidthAdjustment": 0.0,
        "HeightAdjustment": 0.0,
